 "note": "a castle battlement (art round 13): a parapet 28 high with merlons 44 high, 16 thick, wholly on the OUTSIDE of the edge line (half on the wall's top ledge, half hanging over its outer face on a slab and stepped corbels); the walkway's tile keeps its whole diamond. `<north|west>_<far|near>_*`: far = the walkway is south/east of the edge (outside north/west, the camera's far side: the merlons' inner faces are seen), near = the walkway is north/west (outside south/east: the outer faces and the corbels are seen). Anchors at the tile's top vertex at the walkway's floor, as wall_stone's. Written for a wall on layer 1 (the floor surface 96 over the ground), standing on the village stone wall.. Wired (docs/02, 2026-10-29): which side the walkway is on is derived from the floors of the wall's own layer (src/battlements.js), never stored; the depth plane is the edge line (far) or 16 beyond it (near); no cap, no post (vertex pieces by src/battlements.js)."
